<title>USA: Asheville, N.C., yields 5.825 pct in 2025.</title>
<headline>Asheville, N.C., yields 5.825 pct in 2025.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Robinson Humphrey Co Inc</p>
<p>said Tuesday it tentatively priced $33 million Asheville,</p>
<p>N.C., water system revenue bonds at a top yield of</p>
<p>approximately 5.825 percent in 2025.</p>
<p>The preliminary pricing follows:</p>
<p>ASHEVILLE, N.C.</p>
<p>RE: $33,000,000*</p>
<p>WATER SYSTEM REVENUE BONDS, SERIES 1996</p>
<p>MOODY'S: Aaa (A UNDERLYING)</p>
<p>S&amp;P: AAA (A UNDERLYING)</p>
<p>FGIC INSURED</p>
<p>DATED: 9/15/1996</p>
<p>FIRST COUPON: 2/1/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 8/1</p>
<p>    8/1	     Amount	  Coupon	Price</p>
<p>    Maturity	(million)	   (pct)	 (% of par)</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    1999	    $0.050	  4.40	  100</p>
<p>    2000	    $0.110	  4.50	  100</p>
<p>    2001	    $0.160	  4.60	  100</p>
<p>    2002	    $0.540	  4.70	  100</p>
<p>    2003	    $0.680	  4.80	  100</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    2004	    $0.765	  4.90	  100</p>
